  "body": "### Finding description and impact\n\nThe invariant intended to enforce a minimum reward-per-epoch distribution is incorrectly computed in _createCampaign() inside DistributionCreator. The check uses the before fee removal campaign amount instead of the after fee removal distributed amount, allowing creators to bypass the minimum amount distributed per-epoch requirement.\n\n### Root cause\n\nDuring campaign creation, the protocol applies fees to the reward amount:\n\n```solidity\nuint256 fee = (amount * feeBps) / 1e9;\nuint256 distributedAmount = amount - fee;\n```\n\nHowever, the invariant meant to enforce sufficient reward per epoch is evaluated using the original amount, not the distributedAmount:\n```solidity\n// Incorrect invariant\nrequire((amount * EPOCH_DURATION) / duration >= rewardTokenMinAmounts[token]);\n```\n\nThis produces a logical mismatch:\n\t•\tThe check verifies that the pre-fee amount per epoch exceeds the minimum threshold.\n\t•\tBut the actual tokens delivered to the Distributor are reduced by fees, resulting in a lower real distribution per epoch.\n\nThe PoC demonstrates this flaw:\n\t1.\tA user chooses a reward amount just above the minimum-per-epoch threshold.\n\t2.\tAfter fee deduction, the real amount becomes lower than the required minimum.\n\t3.\tThe campaign still passes validation because the invariant used the higher pre-fee value.\n\nAs a result, a campaign can be created with underfunded per-epoch rewards, violating the economic guarantees the invariant was supposed to enforce.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis vulnerability enables systematic circumvention of the minimum reward-per-epoch constraints:\n\t•\tCampaign creators can intentionally select an amount that barely meets the invariant, knowing that fees will push the real distribution below the enforced minimum.\n\t•\tUnderfunded distributions may lead to:\n\t•\tInadequate per epoch incentives.\n\t•\tMisleading campaign configurations passed off as compliant.\n\t•\tPotential downstream issues for users expecting a minimum guaranteed payout.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n1. Perform invariant checks on the post-fee distributed amount\n\nReplace the current invariant with one using distributedAmount, not amount:\n```solidity\nuint256 fee = (amount * feeBps) / BASE_9;\nuint256 distributedAmount = amount - fee;\n\nrequire(\n    (distributedAmount * EPOCH_DURATION) / duration >= rewardTokenMinAmounts[token],\n    \"Distributed amount per epoch below minimum\"\n);\n```\nThis ensures the check aligns with the actual amount available for reward distribution.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n\nimport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/IERC20Metadata.sol\";\nimport { DistributionCreator } from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { Distributor, MerkleTree } from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n    Distributor internal distributor;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        distributor = Distributor(deployUUPS(address(new Distributor()), hex\"\"));\n        distributor.initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControlManager)));\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n /// @dev PoC showing that fee deductions let campaigns under-deliver per-epoch rewards below the enforced minimum.\n    function testPoC_feeDeductionBypassesMinInvariant() external {\n        uint32 duration = EPOCH_DURATION;\n        uint32 startTimestamp = uint32(block.timestamp + EPOCH_DURATION);\n        uint256 minPerEpoch = creator.rewardTokenMinAmounts(address(angle));\n        uint256 defaultFees = creator.defaultFees();\n        assertGt(defaultFees, 0, \"Default fee must be set\");\n\n        // Force a final distribution amount just above the minimum by inflating the pre-fee value\n        uint256 targetDistributedAmount = (minPerEpoch * duration) / EPOCH_DURATION - 1;\n        uint256 preFeeAmount = (targetDistributedAmount * 1e9) / (1e9 - defaultFees) + 1;\n\n        CampaignParameters memory params = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: alice,\n            rewardToken: address(angle),\n            amount: preFeeAmount,\n            campaignType: 0,\n            startTimestamp: startTimestamp,\n            duration: duration,\n            campaignData: abi.encode(\"fee bypass\")\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(params);\n        CampaignParameters memory storedCampaign = creator.campaign(campaignId);\n\n        uint256 distributedPerEpoch = (storedCampaign.amount * EPOCH_DURATION) / storedCampaign.duration;\n        assertLt(distributedPerEpoch, minPerEpoch, \"Distributed amount after fees is below minimum\");\n    }\n\n}\n```",
